  {
    "episode_id": 80456,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/0/80456.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "The role of governor, governor in the state of Ohio is massive, broad. It reaches into so much of what goes on in the Buckeye state. So as you just kind of look at the major functions of the office of governor, what are some of the big things that you feel are most important the governor should do for the citizens of Ohio?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "The role of governor in the state of Ohio is massive.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "The role of governor in the state of Ohio is broad.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "The role of governor in the state of Ohio reaches into many aspects of life in Ohio.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "There are major functions associated with the office of governor.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker is asking the listener to identify key responsibilities of the governor for Ohio citizens.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "The governor holds significant influence over state affairs in Ohio.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "The listener has relevant knowledge about the duties of the Ohio governor.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "The importance of the governor’s role is widely recognized within Ohio political discourse.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Citizens of Ohio expect the governor to play a central role in addressing their needs.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Public expectations about governance include proactive leadership by the governor.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Topic Shift"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 80456,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/0/80456.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think a governor has to listen a lot and travel and talk with people. I do that. No one's traveled the state, probably more than I have in the last 30 years or so. And every single day, I'm out talking with people and listening. I learn things from the people of the state. So governor, first of all, I think it's got to be a good listener. Governor has to lead. I've tried to make it very clear throughout this campaign where I want to lead the State of Ohio. We have a full full plan. I would invite any of our listeners to go up on our webpage, mikedewine.com. And you will see our jobs plan, our education plan plan for children, our anti drug efforts. And those go into probably more detail than we're going to be able to go into on the show. But as I look at Where Ohio needs to go, I think we've come a long way in the last eight years. Eight years ago, we had 400,000 people who had lost their jobs. We had a difficult circumstance situation with our budget, 89 cents in the rainy day fund. I mean a lot of problems, but we've come a long way in eight years and our goal now is to take Ohio to the next level and we're going to focus on the really jobs. I think the number one job of a governor is to create a climate in the state that is a pro jobs, pro growth environment. You do that by keeping taxes down. You do that by keeping regulations. rational and reasonable and not excessive. You create that business climate in the state, but you go beyond that and we can talk about it further, but it's education. We have to fill the skills gap that we have in Ohio. We have to do a better job educating young people. We have to do a better job. People who are in mid-career and lose their job or need to move, we need to do a better job helping them and get the skills that they need to move forward. And we have to really deal with the drug problem. We have a comprehensive plan which we can talk about in more detail in regard to what we're going to do with the drug problem.",
