  {
    "episode_id": 80456,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/0/80456.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 19,
    "turn_text": "Mr. Mike DeWine, our guest on Town Hall, Ohio, the Republican candidate for governor. We'll be back to you here more with him in just a few moments and remind you that next week at this time, Democratic challenger Richard Cordray will be our guest and he'll talk to you about his aspirations to be our next governor. A note from the Ohio Farm Bureau election guide in the column by Ohio Farm Bureau's President Frank Burkett telling you why you need to be paying attention and getting engaged. It points out that in the election, a primary election last May, there were 59 races decided by a single vote, and over the last five years, 199 races in Ohio, where a single vote would have changed the outcome. As President Birkett says, your vote matters. Farm votes matter, so make sure you study up and then show up on election day. you For our last two pre-election shows, we're hearing from the two candidates for Ohio governor. This week, it's Republican Mike DeWine. Next week, it will be Democrat Richard Cordray. So let's get back to our conversation as Mike DeWine visited with town hall Ohio listeners in the Ohio Farm Bureau studio. So Mr. DeWine, let's follow up on some of the economic challenges that you pointed out. We're doing okay. We always want to do better. When you look at the tools that state government can employ to boost the Ohio economy, what are some of the appropriate ones that your administration would consider?",
