    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/0/80456.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "Well, first of all, you're absolutely right whether a business wants to expand who's already in Ohio or whether a business is looking to come to Ohio. If they don't think they can find employees who have the skill sets who can pass the drug test, they're not coming or they're not going to expand. So I've talked to many businesses in Ohio who say, look, we're kind of stuck where we are because we don't think we can get the employees. Education is number one. The state also can play a role with Jobs Ohio. Jobs Ohio is something that Governor Kasich and the state legislature created. It is really taking the economic development arm of the state and privatized it, gives them more flexibility. And I think it's worked pretty well. What I want to make sure is that Jobs Ohio is available for all 88 counties. So if you live in a rural county, You know, Jobs, Ohio needs to be there available for you and the employers in that county to expand jobs. It should not be just something that we look at is for Columbus and Cleveland and Cincinnati or some other big city. So it should be there for every single part of the state.",
