  {
    "episode_id": 80456,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/0/80456.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 32,
    "turn_text": "Well, very, very good question. First of all, let me address something that my opponent in this campaign that keep running ads about, which are simply not true. And that has to do with preexisting illness. I am for coverage of preexisting illnesses. In fact, not once, not twice, not three times, but seven separate times I have voted in favor of coverage for preexisting illness. So that is a very, very important thing. Number two, we have a problem with middlemen, PBMs, they're called, who are making too much money, frankly. We're going to climb government of the state. We are going to tackle that. Medicaid, for example, the state is a huge buyer of drugs to Medicaid in other ways. We're going to work to really get the price down by going after and getting better contracts with these middlemen. In many cases, actually eliminating these middlemen. So that I think is very important. The other thing that we're going to do is really put an emphasis on wellness. Money spent early to get people, you know, well, to keep them well is money that is very, very well spent and will save tax dollars in the long run.",
