    "turn_idx": 34,
    "turn_text": "Well, we have to use science, first of all. Everything we do has to be dictated by what we know. Ohio State's Stone Lab, which I was able to get money for when I was in the United States. Congress continues to do very good research. The legislature provided them money in the last Bill that was passed a few months ago, that's very important. So number one, whatever we do has to be based on good science. As governor, I will pull people together. I will pull people together who are concerned about Lake Erie along with the agriculture community. You know, if you look at Northwest Ohio, we have an amazing agriculture community. We have great, great farmland. So we do not want to see our small farmers and our midsize farmers have to go out of business because of over-regulation. So what I support is a bond issue that's been proposed by Randy Gardner in the state legislature. I will champion that as governor of the state. It will be a $1 billion bond issue that will give us the money that we need for the next 10 years. to really go after this problem to make sure the farmers aren't the ones who are bearing all of the burden on what they have to do. We have to clean up Lake Erie. We have to deal with the algae bloom problem, the phosphorus problem. But we have to do that by working together. And that's what I will do. We'll bring farmers to the table. We will work together and with the money from this bond issue, I think it's something that we can really tackle, really make a difference, but also not make the farmers pay in an ordinate amount and bear all the burden of this.",
