  {
    "episode_id": 80456,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/0/80456.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 41,
    "turn_text": "Now, I've been very careful not to over-promise things that I cannot do or that I'm not sure I'm going to be able to do. What I will say is this, that I started my career as a county prosecutor. I fully understand that local government is very, very important. And frankly, that's how we deliver most of our services in the state of Ohio's to the local government. So I will be a friend. I will be a partner to local government. We will help them in certain areas where we've already laid it out. For example, one of the great tragedies is the number of kids who are in foster care, and they're in foster care because of the fact that their parents, one or both parents are drug addicts. That half the kids in foster care today are there because one of the parents are drug addict. So our children's services, our local child welfare systems are overtaxed, overtaxed in the sense of overworked. We are the fiftieth state out of fiftieth union as far as giving money to our local Children's Services. We will change that time, Governor. We will have more money, a significant amount, more money to local children's services. So we will help in that way. We will also help with more resources being available for the drug fight that we will get down to the local communities. So these are two specific ways that we're going to help local government.",
