    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/0/80456.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 43,
    "turn_text": "Well there's no doubt we have infrastructure needs and if we talk about economic development it is very important that infrastructure be taken care of because once again companies won't come to a state where the infrastructure is mass. And so we have to work on this. One of the things that we're going to have to do is have a discussion with the people of the State of Ohio in regard to Ohio Department of Transportation. You know, we're moving now from cars that run on gasoline to cars that run partially or completely, you know, on electricity. And so we have historically paid for our roads based on a gas tax. And that has been really a user tax that has been a pretty fair way to distribute the burden. We need as we move into the different world, we need to make sure that we are adjusting how we make sure that everyone who is drives on our highways does in fact pay a fair share.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
