  {
    "episode_id": 80456,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/0/80456.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 46,
    "turn_text": "Mike Dwein, the Republican candidate for governor and a reminder at this time next week. Richard Cordray, the Democratic Governor candidate will be joining us for Town Hall, Ohio. Also like to remind you that if you'd like information beyond what you're hearing on Town Hall, Ohio, Ohio Farm Bureau's Political Action Committee, the Agriculture for Good Government Political Action Committee, has a great website that answers a lot of questions. Visit farmboatsmatter.org. Welcome back to Town Hall, Ohio, where we are about to conclude our conversation with Mike DeWine, the Republican candidate for Ohio Governor. Mr. DeWine, very kind, to spend an hour in the studio and visiting with Town Hall, Ohio listeners. His opponent was just as courteous. Richard Cordray was in our offices and spent some time with us. We will be hearing Mr. Cordray answering the same questions we're discussing with Mike DeWine. Mr. Cordray will be on at this time next week. As we close out today's show, a question that I have posed to all of our candidates that are in for the statewide office shows, and that deals with civility or lack of civility in our public discourse over political issues. Ask Mr. DeWine, how do we get here and how do we get out?",
