  {
    "episode_id": 80456,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/0/80456.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 52,
    "turn_text": "I have a real vision for where I want to take this state. My experience has been that when you go into office, you better know where you want to go. Again, we would invite anyone to look at this. We lay it out, mikedewine.com, where we want to take the state of Ohio. We want to focus on jobs. We want to make Ohio the number one state in the Midwest for a place to raise your family, number one place to grow a business, number one place. If you're contemplating Moving to a state and creating a business, we want Ohio to be that place. We do it by keeping taxes down. We do it by focusing on keeping the regulations rational and reasonable. We need to have a business friendly environment. We need to also, frankly, fully understand that our agriculture community remains the number one industry in the state of Ohio. I'm someone who not only has farmland and lives on a farm, but someone who is in the seed business, and my parents were, my grandparents, so we really, I think, have a pretty good appreciation for the challenges that agriculture farmers have out there. And I want to be their partner and the partner for everyone in the state. We will do this by bringing people together. I have a long record of bringing people together to make a difference in getting things done and fixing problems. That's what I'll do as governor. I would appreciate our listeners vote. Thank you very much.",
